## 5. Preferences and working style — carry these forward exactly

These are the PM's standing preferences, confirmed and re-confirmed
across two full sessions now. Follow them without being asked.

- **Mock up before building, every time**, using real screenshots of the
  actual built site with the real webfonts loaded (see §9 — this is not
  optional, default-system fonts give misleading measurements). Never use
  the interactive widget/diagramming tool for this project — PNG mockups
  only, clearly labelled "MOCKUP ONLY — do not upload," never mixed in
  with real files.
- **The PM cannot see inline images reliably in this chat surface** —
  files must be attached with `present_files` (or whatever the current
  tool is), not just referenced. Twice this session I described a mockup
  without attaching it and had to be told "can't see it" or "just a
  screenshot" before resending. **Attach every visual you claim to show.**
- **The PM wants direct GitHub links pasted in the chat itself**, not
  buried in a downloadable instructions file — "just list all the links
  here in the chat so I can click them in order" was said explicitly.
  Give: the link, the file it replaces, expected line count, first line.
- **New files first, numbered, with safe stopping points** between
  logical groups (this mattered a lot in the spacing batch; less relevant
  once we moved to one-file-at-a-time live iteration this session, but
  keep it in mind for any future multi-file batch).
- **Never paste raw code into the chat** — always a downloadable file.
- **A CMS hard-refresh reminder whenever `config.yml` changes** — several
  times this session (registration status, headline-optional) needed
  this; keep flagging it.
- **The PM will correct you plainly and expects you to actually find the
  real cause, not just try another guess.** The logo saga (§6) is the
  clearest example: two "fixes" in a row treated the symptom differently
  without diagnosing it, and the PM's third message — "maybe it's because
  you're aligning the outer edges of the stars in the logo, and not the
  type?" — was the correct diagnosis, handed to me. When a PM correction
  suggests a specific mechanism, take it seriously and verify it before
  trying yet another surface-level tweak.
- **Always verify the actual rendered pixels, not just the CSS you wrote.**
  The logo saga's second bug (the `max-width: 100%` squash) was invisible
  in the CSS and only showed up by measuring the rendered image's width
  against its intended aspect ratio. Several other times this session,
  computed-style checks (via a headless browser) caught mismatches that
  reading the CSS alone would have missed — e.g. a leftover `0.88rem`
  media-query rule that silently overrode the Donate button's font-size
  after it looked correct in the file. **Screenshot AND measure, every
  time, before presenting something as fixed.**
- **Never claim something is fixed without having rebuilt and re-measured
  it.** Standard workflow this session, every single change: edit → clean
  rebuild → serve locally with the real webfonts → screenshot and/or
  measure with a headless browser → only then say it's done.
- **The PM approves incrementally and iterates live** — today was a
  single flowing session of many small requests against the live preview,
  not a batch handover. Be ready for "no, still not right, try X" as a
  normal part of the workflow, not a sign of failure — see the logo saga.

