## 9. Technical setup notes (carried forward from the morning handover,
    still true)

- **Google Fonts is unreachable from the sandbox** — Archivo Black,
  Baloo 2, and Source Sans 3 will NOT load in a headless browser unless
  served locally. Every screenshot/measurement this session used real
  `.ttf` files fetched from the Google Fonts GitHub mirror and served
  from a local `testfonts/` folder alongside each build, with an
  `@font-face` override injected before measuring.
  `document.fonts.check()` is not sufficient — it returns true even for a
  fallback font. Re-fetch these fonts at the start of a new session; they
  don't persist between sessions.
- **Local build/serve pattern that worked reliably**: `npm run build`,
  then `setsid nohup python3 -m http.server <port> --directory <path>/dist
  > /tmp/h<port>.log 2>&1 < /dev/null &` (plain `nohup &` without `setsid`
  was unreliable — the server sometimes died between tool calls). Always
  `curl` to confirm the server actually answers before trusting a
  Playwright screenshot.
- **Playwright (via Python) was used throughout** for both screenshots and
  precise pixel measurement (`getBoundingClientRect()`,
  `getComputedStyle()`) — this combination is what caught the two logo
  bugs that would have been invisible from a screenshot alone.

